## 8. Technical implementation requirements

### Quality standards (MUST)

- Music theory respected: rhythmic variety, phrase lengths in 4 / 8 / 16 bars
- Velocity, timing and filter automation so nothing sounds mechanical
- Proper gain staging, EQ separation and bus compression
- Fade-in/out and click-free edits (zero-crossing or short crossfades)
- In terms of the theory mastery, knowledge and approach: inspiration from the classical music, from traditional/folk music etc., applying and adjusting the best practices seamlessly for the composition of your target genre

### Amateurish approaches to AVOID (MUST NOT)

- Copy-pasted identical loops for the whole length
- Pure sine / default waveform sounds with no envelopes or filtering
- Everything quantised perfectly with equal velocities
- Clipping, DC offset or clicks at loop and section boundaries
- Muddy mix with all instruments in the same frequency range

